---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Returns & Refunds"
  description="Returns and refunds information for Woodfox Coffee orders."
  updated="October 14, 2026"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Online ordering is not yet available.</strong> This page describes how returns and refunds will work once
    it opens. Highlighted details will be confirmed before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <p>
    Coffee is a food product, so for safety reasons we can’t accept returns of opened bags. If something isn’t right
    with your order, we want to know.
  </p>

  <h2>Damaged, incorrect or missing items</h2>
  <p>
    If your order arrives damaged, incorrect or incomplete, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    within <mark class="confirm">[owner to confirm, e.g. 14 days]</mark> of delivery with your order number and, where
    possible, a photo. We’ll send a replacement or issue a refund.
  </p>

  <h2>If you don’t enjoy a coffee</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="confirm">[Owner to decide: e.g. one-time credit or replacement for a first-time purchase, or no refunds on
    taste preference.]</mark>
  </p>

  <h2>Unopened bags</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="confirm">[Owner to decide whether unopened bags may be returned, the time limit, and who pays return
    shipping.]</mark>
  </p>

  <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    You’ll be able to skip, pause or cancel a subscription before your next billing date
    <mark class="confirm">[owner to confirm cut-off, e.g. 2 days before]</mark>. Shipments already processed can’t be
    cancelled.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are issued</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are returned to the original payment method through our payment provider. Timing depends on your
    bank <mark class="confirm">[owner to confirm typical timeframe]</mark>.
  </p>

  <h2>Wholesale</h2>
  <p>Returns and credits for wholesale partners follow the terms agreed with each account.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about an order? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
